issue_context.body:
**Describe the bug**
I believe commit [42036cd](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/commit/42036cdbcae270d00b5bd08e805e33bbd3b5787f) broke the ability of Meta-IRQs to preempt all other threads even if those are cooperative. This was working as expected in Zephyr 3.5.0

```
Z_GENERIC_SECTION(.text._HandlerModeExit) void z_arm_exc_exit(void)
{
#ifdef CONFIG_PREEMPT_ENABLED
	/* If thread is preemptible */
	if (_kernel.cpus->current->base.prio >= 0) {
		/* and cached thread is not current thread */
		if (_kernel.ready_q.cache != _kernel.cpus->current) {
			/* trigger a context switch */
			SCB->ICSR |= SCB_ICSR_PENDSVSET_Msk;
		}
	}
#endif /* CONFIG_PREEMPT_ENABLED */
```
`if (_kernel.cpus->current->base.prio >= 0)` prevents the meta-IRQ from being woken when returning from an interrupt unblocking it with e.g sem_give()

The "promise" as stated in the documentation is broken: 
_The thread, once woken, will be guaranteed to run before the current CPU returns into application code._

**To Reproduce**
Have a cooperative thread doing some processing and have a meta-IRQ thread waiting for a semaphore. Unblock the meta-IRQ by calling a sem_give() from IRQ context. The meta-irq will not be woken immediately but I believe at the first possible reschedule point. 


**Expected behavior**
The meta-IRQ should preempt the cooperative thread and after processing return to that cooperative thread.  

**Impact**
(Severe impact) In our case, we are collected data from a front-end in a time-critical manner  (10ms interval) while also running Bluetooth host. Since BT_RX_WQ is a  cooperative thread the meta-IRQ cannot be woken within the time frame especially when connection is being established. 


**Environment :**

 - Zephyr 3.7.0
